{
  "mn65:0.1": "Middle Discourses 65 ",
  "mn65:0.2": "With Bhaddāli ",
  "mn65:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn65:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn65:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn65:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn65:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn65:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn65:2.1": "“Mendicants, I eat my food in one sitting per day. ",
  "mn65:2.2": "Doing so, I find that I’m healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably. ",
  "mn65:2.3": "You too should eat your food in one sitting per day. ",
  "mn65:2.4": "Doing so, you’ll find that you’re healthy and well, nimble, strong, and living comfortably.” ",
  "mn65:3.1": "When he said this, Venerable Bhaddāli said to the Buddha, ",
  "mn65:3.2": "“Sir, I’m not going to attempt to eat my food in one sitting per day. ",
  "mn65:3.3": "For when eating once a day I might feel remorse and regret.” ",
  "mn65:4.1": "“Well then, Bhaddāli, eat one part of the meal in the place where you’re invited, and bring the rest back to eat. ",
  "mn65:4.2": "Eating this way, too, you will sustain yourself.” ",
  "mn65:4.3": "“Sir, I’m not going to attempt to eat that way, either. ",
  "mn65:4.4": "For when eating that way I might also feel remorse and regret.” ",
  "mn65:4.5": "Then, as this rule was being laid down by the Buddha and the Saṅgha was undertaking it, Bhaddāli announced he would